# ThaalDraft V2 — Implementation Roadmap

## Phase 0 — Reset and Audit

Goal:

- freeze current chaos
- align architecture
- identify broken flows
- remove duplicated logic

Deliverables:

- ARCHITECTURE_V2.md
- PRD_V2.md
- UI_UX_V2.md
- DATABASE_SCHEMA_V2.sql
- implementation checklist

Acceptance:

- team agrees on one source of truth
- Canonical Manuscript JSON is defined

---

## Phase 1 — Document Intelligence Layer

Goal:

- support messy input
- extract text, images, tables, metadata, and styles

DOCX:

- unzip `.docx`
- parse XML
- parse styles
- extract media files

PDF:

- PyMuPDF
- OCR fallback
- layout-aware extraction

Deliverables:

- docx extractor
- pdf extractor
- markdown extractor
- latex extractor
- extraction report

Acceptance:

- uploaded file can be decomposed into structured fragments

---

## Phase 2 — Canonical Manuscript JSON

Goal:

- build one consistent manuscript model

Must include:

- title
- authors
- affiliations
- abstract
- keywords
- sections
- figures
- tables
- references
- citations
- DOI metadata

Deliverables:

- manuscript schema
- serializer
- validator
- persistence layer

Acceptance:

- all downstream modules read the same model

---

## Phase 3 — Structure Intelligence

Goal:

- reconstruct manuscript structure from messy drafts

Use:

- spaCy
- Sentence Transformers
- Gemini first
- DeepSeek second

Tasks:

- section detection
- author detection
- affiliation detection
- abstract detection
- reference detection
- figure/table association

Deliverables:

- structure engine
- reconstruction report
- confidence scoring

Acceptance:

- manuscript can be reconstructed even if headings are inconsistent or partially missing

---

## Phase 4 — DOI and Citation Intelligence

Goal:

- validate and enrich references

Integrations:

- CrossRef
- OpenAlex
- Semantic Scholar

Tasks:

- DOI extraction
- DOI lookup
- citation style detection
- reference validation
- missing citation detection
- duplicate citation detection

Deliverables:

- citation report
- DOI report
- enrichment workflow

Acceptance:

- references are validated against real APIs

---

## Phase 5 — Reviewer AI

Goal:

- generate actionable review feedback

AI Priority:

- Gemini
- DeepSeek fallback

Tasks:

- writing quality
- novelty
- structure quality
- publication readiness
- missing section warnings

Deliverables:

- review report
- readiness score
- actionable suggestions

Acceptance:

- review output is useful and readable

---

## Phase 6 — Formatting Studio

Goal:

- convert manuscripts into publication-ready formats

Support:

- IEEE
- Elsevier
- Springer
- ACM
- APA
- MLA
- Nature
- Custom journal formatting

Tasks:

- template-driven formatting
- style conversion
- citation formatting
- heading formatting
- table/figure formatting

Deliverables:

- format engine
- template system
- formatting validation

Acceptance:

- one manuscript can be exported into multiple publication styles

---

## Phase 7 — Export Engine

Goal:

- produce downloadable outputs

Outputs:

- DOCX
- PDF
- LaTeX
- ZIP package

Deliverables:

- download endpoints
- export history
- file naming rules

Acceptance:

- every completed format has a download path

---

## Phase 8 — Workspace and UI Modernization

Goal:

- replace current UI with V2 workspace

Requirements:

- hybrid workspace
- progress states
- live status updates
- dynamic module cards
- error recovery
- no dead buttons

Deliverables:

- new dashboard
- new document view
- new formatting studio
- new reports view

Acceptance:

- UI changes with backend progress

---

## Phase 9 — Batch Processing and Submission Package

Goal:

- support multi-file workflows

Tasks:

- batch upload
- batch queue
- batch status
- submission ZIP
- cover letter
- author statement

Deliverables:

- batch manager
- submission builder
- package downloader

Acceptance:

- multi-document workflow works end to end

---

## Phase 10 — Testing and Deployment

Goal:

- verify production readiness

Must test:

- upload
- extraction
- reconstruction
- citations
- DOI
- review
- formatting
- export
- UI refresh

Deliverables:

- test report
- validation report
- deployment checklist

Acceptance:

- no silent failures
- no broken workflows
- no fake completion states
